---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import Navbar from "../components/Navbar.astro";
import Footer from "../components/Footer.astro";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Privacy Policy"
  description="Apps for Change Privacy Policy. Learn how we collect, use, and protect your information across our free mobile apps."
>
  <Navbar />
  <main class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8 py-12 sm:py-16">
    <h1 class="text-3xl sm:text-4xl mb-2">Privacy Policy</h1>
    <p class="text-(--color-text-secondary) mb-8">Effective Date: September 19, 2026</p>

    <section class="mb-10">
      <h2 class="text-xl sm:text-2xl mb-3">Our Commitment to You</h2>
      <p>
        Apps for Change is a Minnesota-based 501(c)(3) nonprofit. We build free mobile apps to help people
        reach goals, practice self-advocacy, stay connected, and build healthier habits. This policy explains
        in plain language what each app stores, what is synced to our servers, and what is never collected.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="mb-10">
      <h2 class="text-xl sm:text-2xl mb-3">1. Who We Are</h2>
      <p>
        Apps for Change is a nonprofit organization incorporated in Minnesota. Our apps are free. We do not
        sell, rent, or trade personal information, and we do not use your data for advertising.
      </p>
      <p class="mt-2">
        Website: <a href="https://appsforchange.org" class="text-(--color-accent) hover:underline">appsforchange.org</a>
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="mb-10">
      <h2 class="text-xl sm:text-2xl mb-3">2. How Data Works in Each App</h2>
      <p class="mb-4">
        Our apps do <strong>not</strong> all work the same way. Please read the section for the app you use.
      </p>

      <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold mb-2">Advocate's Compass</h3>
      <p class="mb-4">
        Meeting prep notes, skills progress, and preferences stay <strong>on your device</strong>
        (AsyncStorage). There is no account, no cloud backup, and no cloud AI. Advocate Now uses built-in
        offline templates. Uninstalling the app removes this data.
      </p>

      <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold mb-2">Goal Getter</h3>
      <p class="mb-4">
        Creating an account (email or sign-in provider) is required so your goals, milestones, tasks,
        calendar items, and life-area progress can sync to our backend. That data is stored on our hosted
        application server so it is available when you sign in on another device.
      </p>

      <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold mb-2">Care About You</h3>
      <p class="mb-4">
        An account is required. Contacts you add, planned acts of kindness, and completion status sync to
        our backend. Optional <strong>AI suggestions</strong> send the selected contact’s name, your notes,
        and recent task history to a language-model provider so the app can suggest a next kindness. You
        trigger this only when you tap to generate insights or suggestions.
      </p>

      <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold mb-2">Beat the Craving</h3>
      <p class="mb-4">
        An account is required. Your craving counter and coping-option list (including custom options) sync
        to our backend so they persist across devices. The counter increases when you choose a coping
        option, not when you merely open the app. This is wellness tracking, not medical advice
        and not a diagnostic tool.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="mb-10">
      <h2 class="text-xl sm:text-2xl mb-3">3. What Information We Collect</h2>

      <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold mb-2">Information you give us</h3>
      <ul class="list-disc pl-6 mb-4 space-y-1">
        <li>Name and email, if you create an account (Goal Getter, Care About You, Beat the Craving)</li>
        <li>Content you enter in the app (goals, tasks, contacts, notes, coping options)</li>
        <li>Messages you send to our support or idea inboxes</li>
      </ul>

      <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold mb-2">Information collected automatically</h3>
      <ul class="list-disc pl-6 mb-4 space-y-1">
        <li>Basic device and app version information needed to run the app</li>
        <li>Crash or error reports in development builds (production apps should not send logs to third-party debug tools)</li>
        <li>Website traffic on appsforchange.org may use standard hosting analytics</li>
      </ul>

      <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold mb-2">Information we do not collect</h3>
      <ul class="list-disc pl-6 space-y-1">
        <li>Precise location</li>
        <li>Your phone contacts, photos, or files (unless you later grant a permission we have not enabled today)</li>
        <li>Payment card numbers in the apps (donations, when enabled, are processed by Stripe on this website)</li>
        <li>Advertising identifiers for ads — we do not run ads</li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <section class="mb-10">
      <h2 class="text-xl sm:text-2xl mb-3">4. How We Use Your Information</h2>
      <ul class="list-disc pl-6 mb-4 space-y-1">
        <li>Provide the features you asked for (sync, reminders you enable, AI suggestions you request)</li>
        <li>Keep you signed in and recover your account</li>
        <li>Fix bugs and improve the apps</li>
        <li>Respond to support requests</li>
      </ul>
      <p>We do not sell, rent, or trade your personal information. We do not use it for advertising.</p>
    </section>

    <section class="mb-10">
      <h2 class="text-xl sm:text-2xl mb-3">5. Who Processes Data for Us</h2>
      <p class="mb-4">
        We use service providers only to operate the apps and this website. They may process data only to
        provide that service to us:
      </p>
      <ul class="list-disc pl-6 mb-4 space-y-1">
        <li><strong>Application hosting / auth</strong> — Goal Getter, Care About You, and Beat the Craving currently run on hosted backends at <code>*.app.specular.dev</code> with Better Auth for accounts.</li>
        <li><strong>AI (Care About You only)</strong> — optional suggestion features send the selected contact context to Anthropic via that host. Do not enter information you would not want a processor to see.</li>
        <li><strong>Payments (website)</strong> — if donations are enabled, Stripe processes the payment. We do not store your full card number.</li>
        <li><strong>Email</strong> — messages you send to support or info inboxes are handled as ordinary email.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>We may also disclose information if required by law, or to protect the safety of our users or the public.</p>
    </section>

    <section class="mb-10">
      <h2 class="text-xl sm:text-2xl mb-3">6. Data Storage and Security</h2>
      <p class="mb-3">
        <strong>Advocate's Compass</strong> stores your entries on the device only.
      </p>
      <p class="mb-3">
        <strong>Goal Getter, Care About You, and Beat the Craving</strong> store account and app content on
        our hosted servers so the apps can sync. We use HTTPS and restrict access to people who operate the
        service. No system is perfectly secure; please use a unique password.
      </p>
      <p>
        If you delete an account or uninstall an on-device-only app, associated data is removed from that
        product as described in the app. Email us if you need help deleting a cloud account.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="mb-10">
      <h2 class="text-xl sm:text-2xl mb-3">7. Data Retention</h2>
      <p>
        On-device data is under your control (clear app data or uninstall). Account data is kept while your
        account is open, then deleted or de-identified when you ask us to close it, unless we must keep a
        limited record for legal or security reasons. Crash reports are kept only as long as needed to fix
        issues.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="mb-10">
      <h2 class="text-xl sm:text-2xl mb-3">8. Children's Privacy</h2>
      <p>
        Our apps are for a general audience and are not directed at children under 13. We do not knowingly
        collect personal information from children under 13. If you believe a child under 13 has created an
        account, contact us and we will delete it.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="mb-10">
      <h2 class="text-xl sm:text-2xl mb-3">9. Your Rights and Choices</h2>
      <ul class="list-disc pl-6 mb-4 space-y-1">
        <li>Access and review data you entered in the app</li>
        <li>Correct or delete entries in the app</li>
        <li>Sign out, or request account deletion by email</li>
        <li>Decline optional AI features in Care About You by not tapping generate</li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        Privacy questions: <a href="mailto:support@appsforchange.org" class="text-(--color-accent) hover:underline">support@appsforchange.org</a>.
        We will respond within 30 days.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="mb-10">
      <h2 class="text-xl sm:text-2xl mb-3">10. Cookies and This Website</h2>
      <p>
        The mobile apps do not use advertising cookies. This website may use cookies or logs needed to run
        the site and process donations. We do not use tracking for advertising.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="mb-10">
      <h2 class="text-xl sm:text-2xl mb-3">11. Changes to This Policy</h2>
      <p>
        When we update this policy we will change the effective date above. If we make a material change
        (for example, adding a new cloud processor), we will note it here and, where required, in the app.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="mb-10">
      <h2 class="text-xl sm:text-2xl mb-3">12. Contact Us</h2>
      <address class="not-italic leading-relaxed">
        <strong>Apps for Change</strong><br />
        A Minnesota 501(c)(3) Nonprofit Corporation<br />
        Support / privacy: <a href="mailto:support@appsforchange.org" class="text-(--color-accent) hover:underline">support@appsforchange.org</a><br />
        General: <a href="mailto:info@appsforchange.org" class="text-(--color-accent) hover:underline">info@appsforchange.org</a><br />
        Website: <a href="https://appsforchange.org" class="text-(--color-accent) hover:underline">appsforchange.org</a><br />
        Phone: 763-276-3958<br />
        1670 S Robert St #131<br />
        West Saint Paul, MN 55118
      </address>
    </section>

    <p class="text-center text-(--color-text-secondary) italic mt-12">Apps for Change — Empowering Everyday People Through Technology</p>
  </main>
  <Footer />
</BaseLayout>
